            <ArticleTitle>Achieving Tolerance with Perforin-Secreting Dendritic Cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.molmed.2015.11.008</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1471-4914(15)00226-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dendritic cells (DCs) regulate the generation of effector adaptive immunity and enforce peripheral tolerance. In the October 2015 issue of Immunity, Zlotnikov-Klionsky et al. present exciting data describing a population of perforin-expressing CD11c(+)DCs that limit obesity as well as metabolic and autoimmune inflammation in mice.</AbstractText>
